 :reserved-name-collision
 {:measured "2026-09-08, re-measured 2026-09-10"
  :by "scripts/check-reserved-name-collisions.cljs"
  :finding "Every oracle in this cohort declares a PUBLIC `query`, which the pure S-expression core reserved as a head on 2026-09-06 (lang/guest-grammar.edn :sugar :pure-s-expression-core :forms). 20 of 20 wave-1 pilots across both tranches carry it."
  :surfaced-in "com-aadhaar first, because it was then the sole pilot that had attempted a whole-component build: src/aadhaar/whole_component.kotoba called (query store entity) and (query store entity id), which amu refused with :kotoba.error/pure-query-arity -- `query reads one datom (query entity attribute)`. That refusal is HISTORICAL as of 2026-09-10; see :requalified-2026-09-10 below."
  :not-a-typo "The oracle's own public surface defines query at arity 2 and 3 over a mutable store. A component whose public names intersect the reserved set collides on migration by construction, and `query` is an ordinary name for a data-access function."
  :consequence "CORRECTED 2026-09-10. The word `blocked` was too strong and, left standing, would have priced a rename as a language gap. The collision is a NAMING PRECONDITION every remaining pilot still meets -- 20 of 20 reproduce -- and both pilots that have since written a whole-component build cleared it the same way, by naming the migrated function store-query. What stays true is that the page_limit.kotoba / paginate.kotoba slices compile clean only because they never touch the name, which is one more reason ADR-q9-whole-component-build-migration does not count them as migrations."
  :not-claimed "This is not a defect in admitting the heads, and no repair wave is owed. Measured across every .kotoba/.cljk in the workspace with ignores off, `query` appears in operator position in exactly one file; lam/app/ref appear only in a deliberate probe using them correctly; perform/rel/handle appear nowhere."
  :bearing-on-the-gate "Does not change :implementation-authorized false. It names a precondition that whole-component requalification must clear first -- rename the oracle's public query, or give the migrated component a different public name and record the divergence."  ;; The requalification ADR-2609081400's successor asks for
  ;; (:next-action :requalify-wave-1-pilots-as-whole-component-builds), for the
  ;; two pilots that have one. Re-measured 2026-09-10 rather than read off this
  ;; block, because two of its three claims had moved in two days.
  :requalified-2026-09-10
  {:collision-claim :reproduces
   :collisions 20
   :oracles-scanned 82
   :guests-scanned 157
   :reserved-heads-in-operator-position 0
   :whole-component-builds-written 2
   :which ["orgs/kotoba-lang/com-aadhaar/src/aadhaar/whole_component.kotoba"
           "orgs/kotoba-lang/com-aave/src/aave/whole_component.kotoba"]
   :how-they-cleared-it "Both name the migrated data-access function store-query, which is this block's own second option -- give the migrated component a different public name and record the divergence. The oracle keeps its public query; nothing was renamed in the .cljc."
   :com-aadhaar-disposition "Its own migration-record.edn version 2 (2026-09-09, amu 6ffc1d71) records :partial-and-running, not :blocked. One layer is genuinely blocked and that record names it."
   :the-other-eighteen "Carry page_limit.kotoba / paginate.kotoba slices only. Under ADR-q9-whole-component-build-migration those are not migrations, so the tranche status stays :tranche-pilots-extracted-no-consumer-cutover for them."
   :reproduce "From the superproject root: nbb --classpath orgs/kotoba-lang/text/src <this repo>/scripts/check-reserved-name-collisions.cljs <the 20 pilot directories> --grammar <this repo>/lang/guest-grammar.edn -- exit 1 with COLLISIONS 20. Passing a SHORT directory list is the trap: an empty or wrong list scans a handful of files, reports COLLISIONS 0 and exits 0, which reads exactly like a clean run. Check the SCANNED lines before believing a zero."}
}
 :reader-conditional-divergence-2026-09-10
 {:finding "The oracle these pilots are ports OF is not one program. `as-int` is a reader conditional whose two branches disagree with each other on trailing-garbage input, so `parity with the oracle` is undefined there until a branch is named normative."
  :measured "2026-09-10, by RUNNING both branches rather than reading them"
  :values {:input "12abc"
           :cljs 12       ;; js/parseInt takes the leading digits
           :clj 0         ;; Long/parseLong throws, the catch yields 0
           :artifact 0}   ;; com-abb-robotics whole_component.kotoba, executed
  :within-measurement-control
  {:input " 42 " :cljs 42 :clj 42
   :reading "The branches AGREE on well-formed input and diverge only on trailing garbage. Without this row the divergence could be a broken harness rather than a property of the source."}
  :cohort 20
  :of 20
  :clj-branch-textually-identical true
  :detector-control "The same grep answers no-rc for whole_component.kotoba and for q9-oracle.cljs, so the 20-of-20 is a census and not a stuck predicate."
  :consequence
  "This is a COHORT decision, not a repository one. Every wave-1 pilot carries
   the same conditional and the same :clj text, so whichever branch is declared
   normative settles all twenty at once. It is recorded and NOT resolved here:
   choosing a branch changes what the product does with `12abc`, which is a
   semantic decision about the actor's REST surface and not a migration step.
   Until it is made, a parity harness run under nbb reports a mismatch for this
   input and the same harness on the JVM reports a match -- and neither reading
   is wrong."
  :reproduce
  "Per pilot: `nbb --classpath src:<kotoba-lang/text>/src -e '(require (quote [<ns>.main :as m])) (println (m/as-int \"12abc\") (m/as-int \" 42 \"))'` prints `12 42`. The :clj branch is the same expression under `clojure -M -e` and prints `0 42`. The artifact side is com-abb-robotics/q9-oracle.cljs plus `amu extract-native --symbol oracle-as-int` through tools/kexe_loader.c."}

 :shared-findings
 {:source-boundary
  "The main.cljc files combine domain decisions, orchestration and native/compatibility effects. They must be split by declared imports, exports and native TCB boundary rather than renamed wholesale; non-ambient portions may migrate to Kotoba components."
  :extension-collision
  "schema/*.kotoba is a generated namespace/entity schema DSL, not Clojure-shaped canonical Kotoba source."
  :safe-next-step
  "Rename the schema DSL through its generator and manifest consumers, then extract bounded Kotoba components while retaining explicit native/compatibility adapters and the CLJC oracle. Later tranches may extract provider components with declared lower-level imports."
  :code-migration-performed :all-ten-bounded-pilots
  :schema-extension-remediation-performed true
  :schema-extension ".kotoba-schema"}
